  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kyrgyzstan: Assistance to - and Cooperation with - the General Procuracy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen and modernize the institutional capacity of the General Procuracy of Kyrgyzstan through improved strategic and budgetary planning. 2) To promote gender equality within the General Procuracy&apos;s institutional and administrative structures and enhance women prosecutors&apos; leadership. 3) To strengthen and modernize the General Procuracy&apos;s training capacity, reflective of international human rights standards, and international best practices through enhanced status of the Prosecutors&apos; Training Centre. 4) To enable prosecutors to gain professional knowledge and skills, and apply them in greater compliance with international human rights law.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: General Procuracy; Prosecutors&#x2019; Training Centre at the General Procuracy; General Procuracy and Prosecutors&#x2019; Training Centre staff and individual prosecutors. Indirect beneficiaries: End users of the criminal justice system, including the accused and victims; society at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to improve the criminal justice response in the Kyrgyz Republic by increasing the resource base, capacity, integrity and efficiency of the General Procuracy.</narrative>
  </description>
